# Coldplay - Viva La Vida
#
# Epic 14.9 showcase. Demonstrates every shipped FX paired with the
# new @palette / @during / bars-notation surface. Use this as a
# learn-by-example reference; trim down to a real performance file
# by deleting whatever doesn't suit the venue.
#
# Sections renamed from section1..section12 to musical labels. The
# rewriter's boundary-overlap matching will preserve these renames
# across future `audio_enrich_cues.py --update` runs.

@artist     Coldplay
@title      viva la vida
@default_fx quiet_wash 20 40 80

@bpm        140
@time_sig   4
@key        G#
@mode       major
@duration   4:03.27
@analysis_synced  2026-06-26T23:59:32Z
@analysis_version 1
@analysis_tool    librosa

# --- Palettes ---------------------------------------------------------
# Declared once, referenced anywhere via @name[idx]. Edit a hex value
# here and every cue that uses it shifts.

# Coldplay's Viva-era stage palette: warm orange / amber / cool red.
@palette warm     #C84020, #C8A030, #802010

# Cool counter-palette for verses + bridges.
@palette cool     #080012, #132038, #0d0716

# Royal accent for the chorus drops.
@palette royal    #A02060, #FFC840, #20A0C8

# Single deep-purple for the bridge.
@palette bridge   #501060

# --- Sections (renamed from librosa defaults) -------------------------

@section silence_in  0:00.00  0:01.18  tempo=139.7 loudness=-60.0
@section intro       0:01.18  0:36.83  tempo=139.7 loudness=-16.6
@section verse1      0:36.83  1:10.58  tempo=139.7 loudness=-15.2
@section chorus1     1:10.58  1:37.80  tempo=139.7 loudness=-11.4
@section verse2      1:37.80  2:04.19  tempo=139.7 loudness=-15.2
@section chorus2     2:04.19  2:48.30  tempo=139.7 loudness=-11.6
@section bridge      2:48.30  3:00.95  tempo=139.7 loudness=-16.9
@section chorus3     3:00.95  3:38.06  tempo=139.7 loudness=-10.7
@section outro_a     3:38.06  3:43.18  tempo=139.7 loudness=-15.6
@section outro_b     3:43.18  3:56.37  tempo=139.7 loudness=-29.0
@section fade        3:56.37  3:59.77  tempo=139.7 loudness=-45.6
@section silence_out 3:59.77  4:03.27  tempo=139.7 loudness=-60.0

0:00     stop
0:01     HeaderText: Coldplay
0:01     BodyText: Viva
0:01     drift_wash @cool[0] @cool[2] 4b
0:02     BodyText: Viva La
0:03     BodyText: Viva La Vida
0:08     HeaderText: 
0:08     BodyText: 

0:12.95  BodyText: I used to rule the world
0:13     sparkle_on_beat @cool[1] 25
0:16.83  BodyText: Seas would rise when I gave the word
00:19.23 BodyText: Now in the morning, I sleep alone
00:23.55 BodyText: Sweep the streets I used to own
00:40.54 BodyText: I used to roll the dice
0:44.69  BodyText: Feel the fear in my enemy's eyes
0:47.73  BodyText: Listened as the crowd would sing
0:51.63  BodyText: "Now the old king is dead, long live the king"
0:54.66  BodyText: One minute I held the key
0:58.57  BodyText: Next, the walls were closed on me
1:01.16  BodyText: And I discovered that my castles stand
1:05.53  BodyText: Upon pillars of salt and pillars of sand
01:09.23 BodyText: I hear Jerusalem bells a-ringing
01:09    pulse   @warm[1] 0 2 5 100
01:10    sparkle_on_beat @royal[2] 25
01:13.11 BodyText: Roman cavalry choirs are singing
01:16.57 BodyText: Be my mirror, my sword and shield
01:19.69 BodyText: My missionaries in a foreign field
1:23.36  BodyText: For some reason, I can't explain
1:26.82  BodyText: Once you'd gone, there was never
1:29.45  BodyText: Never an honest word
1:33.36  BodyText: And that was when I ruled the world
1:33.5   sparkle_on_beat @cool[1] 25
1:40     BodyText:
1:49.88  BodyText: It was a wicked and wild wind
01:54.05 BodyText: Blew down the doors to let me in
1:56.83  BodyText: Shattered windows and the sound of drums
2:01.17  BodyText: People couldn't believe what I'd become
2:04.22  BodyText: Revolutionaries wait
2:08.14  BodyText: For my head on a silver plate
02:10.58 BodyText: Just a puppet on a lonely string
2:15.11  BodyText: Oh, who would ever want to be king?
2:19.01  BodyText: I hear Jerusalem bells a-ringing
2:19     pulse   @warm[1] 0 2 5   100
2:20     sparkle_on_beat @royal[2] 25
2:22.45  BodyText: Roman cavalry choirs are singing
2:25.91  BodyText: Be my mirror, my sword and shield
2:29.43  BodyText: My missionaries in a foreign field
2:32.94  BodyText: For some reason, I can't explain
2:36.35  BodyText: I know Saint Peter won't call my name
02:39.64 BodyText: Never an honest word
02:42.71 BodyText: But that was when I ruled the world
2:50     BodyText:
2:55     linear_buildup @royal[1] 100 64 0 --buildup 7
3:00.95  pulse   @warm[1] 0 2 5   100
3:01.5   wash_with_sparkle @warm[0] @royal[0] 2b @royal[1] 100 0
3:15.09  BodyText: Hear Jerusalem bells a-ringing
3:15     pulse   @warm[1] 0 2 5   100
3:18.10  BodyText: Roman cavalry choirs are singing
3:21.54  BodyText: Be my mirror, my sword and shield
3:21.54  group_cascade @royal[2] 100 3
3:25.09  BodyText: My missionaries in a foreign field
3:28.57  BodyText: For some reason, I can't explain
03:32.04 BodyText: I know Saint Peter won't call my name
3:35.32  BodyText: Never an honest word
3:38.38  BodyText: But that was when I ruled the world
3:38     quiet_wash @warm[2] 60 200 0
3:43.18  fade_to_black 255 0 --buildup 8
03:44    BodyText: 

3:58     stop

# =====================================================================
# FX showcase (Epic 14.9). One representative cue per shipped FX,
# with comments explaining what each one does + which Block 14.9
# feature it demonstrates. Mix of @during (section-anchored) and
# timestamp-driven cues so you can see both flows.
# =====================================================================

# --- intro --------------------------------------------------------- #
# drift_wash with bars-notation cycle. Slowly cross-fades cool[0]
# anchor A to cool[1] anchor B over 4 bars (= 4 * 4 * 60000/140 / 100
# = ~69 = ~6.86 s). Setting the FX at section start = ambient bed
# for the whole intro until verse1 replaces it.
# @during intro   drift_wash @cool[0] @cool[1] 4b

# --- verse1 -------------------------------------------------------- #
# Two FX stack at the section start (different channel surfaces, so
# they coexist):
#   quiet_wash     - low-intensity ambient bed
#   pulse_per_bar  - one pulse per bar on group 0 (broadcast) for a
#                    subtle "1, 2, 3, 4" downbeat anchor
# @during verse1  quiet_wash      @cool[0] 100 255 0
#@during verse1  pulse_per_bar   @warm[1] 100 4 0

# --- chorus1 ------------------------------------------------------- #
# wash_with_sparkle is the layered "wash A <-> wash B + sparkle on
# top" FX. Single cue replaces both quiet_wash + sparkle_on_beat
# pair. Bars notation on the cycle (= 2 bars = ~3.4 s).
#@during chorus1 wash_with_sparkle  @warm[0] @warm[1] 2b @royal[2] 80 0

# --- verse2 -------------------------------------------------------- #
# Second verse: drift between two cool tones, slower cycle (8 bars).
# Forward-references chorus[0] for variation - palettes can be
# mixed freely.
#@during verse2  drift_wash @cool[2] @warm[2] 8b

# --- chorus2 ------------------------------------------------------- #
# Bigger chorus: sparkle_on_beat at 100% probability (every beat
# fires) for energy. Layered with quiet_wash underneath as a colour
# bed. Group split: wash broadcast (group 0), sparkle restricted to
# group 1 so a multi-zone fleet has tiered visual depth.
#@during chorus2 quiet_wash       @royal[1] 80 255 0
#@during chorus2 sparkle_on_beat  @royal[2] 100 1

# Halfway through chorus2: group_cascade sweeps the warm[0] colour
# across 3 Lume groups one after the other. Timestamped (not @during)
# because section-start would clash with the sparkle bed above.
#2:25       group_cascade @warm[0] 100 3

# --- bridge -------------------------------------------------------- #
# Bridge: deep purple bed + a one-shot pulse on each lyric anchor.
# Demonstrates timestamp cues for lyric-aligned hits + the pulse FX.
# pulse args: r g b attack(1/10 s) sustain(1/10 s) decay(1/10 s) probability
#@during bridge  quiet_wash @bridge[0] 120 255 0
#2:48.30    pulse @royal[1] 0 2 5 100 0   # "Revolutionaries wait"
#2:54.30    pulse @royal[2] 0 2 5 100 0   # "Just a puppet on a lonely string"

# --- chorus3 (the big one) ----------------------------------------- #
# Build energy INTO the final chorus with linear_buildup over 4 bars
# from start_master 64 to full master at probability 100%. The
# --buildup flag is in seconds and is independent of the FX param
# surface; here 7 s = roughly 4 bars at 140 BPM.
#2:55       linear_buildup @royal[1] 100 64 0 --buildup 7

# Drop: strobe_burst for one bar (= ~1.71 s) at max rate. Used
# sparingly - the 4 Hz cap on the FX prevents Harding-unsafe rates.
#3:00.95    strobe_burst 1b 255 0

# Then the actual chorus3 bed: sparkle_on_beat at high prob.
#3:01.5     wash_with_sparkle @warm[0] @royal[0] 2b @royal[1] 100 0

# Mid-chorus3: brief group_cascade accent on the lyric "Be my mirror"
#3:21.54    group_cascade @royal[2] 100 3

# --- outro_a ------------------------------------------------------- #
# Final wash on the closing line. quiet_wash with reduced intensity.
#@during outro_a  quiet_wash @warm[2] 60 200 0

# --- outro_b ------------------------------------------------------- #
# Fade out over 8 seconds. fade_to_black ramps the master from
# current value to 0 over the --buildup window.
3:43.18    fade_to_black 255 0 --buildup 8

# --- silence_out --------------------------------------------------- #
# Explicit blackout to end the song. `stop` is the parser alias for
# blackout - writes 0 to every channel for one tick.
3:59.77    stop
